/* ===================== v1.60 beta 14 · Personal accounts are an Advanced Couple feature =====================
   Consistency pass over the whole app (Three-Mode Design spec 3.2 / 4 / 9.1 / invariant 10):
   Couple mode = one shared household workspace: household accounts are Shared, visibility is inherited
   from the account, no hide-details / fully-private overrides, and no Private (personal) account can be
   created. Personal (solo) mode shows no Private/Shared labels. Advanced Couple is the only mode with
   Private ("Only me (personal)") accounts. Beta 6/10/11 already gate the accounts manager and the mode
   cards — this layer closes the remaining leaks:
   · R2  Add account outside Advanced Couple can never stay Private (safety net over beta 6/11 wraps).
   · R3  Onboarding person step: the Only me / Shared chooser renders in Advanced Couple only; in Couple
         mode it is removed (beta 6's "Household accounts are shared in Couple mode" hint stays).
   · R4  Onboarding: the default Cash account and the first account are created Private only outside
         Couple mode; in Couple mode they are stripped back to Shared (invariant 10). In Advanced Couple
         a "Shared" choice on the chooser is honoured.
   · R5  Transaction-form privacy pill renders in Advanced Couple only — in Couple mode its hint
         ("to record a Private transaction, use a Private account") cannot be followed and visibility
         is inherited from the shared account anyway.
   · R6  Modes page: the Couple tab now carries the same "Private (Only-me) accounts are available in
         Advanced Couple mode only" line the Personal and Advanced tabs already have (spec 3.2:
         "If private tracking is required inside the same app profile, recommend Advanced Couple Mode").
   · R7  One choose-accounts step everywhere: sharepick now opens share6 (live exposure preview,
         share-history question, Advanced Couple link) — partner-join and the checklist tour included.
   · R8  After choosing accounts in Couple mode, accounts kept "on this device only" trigger the
         plan-9.1 recommendation: compare with Advanced Couple or keep them for now.
   · R9  Copy: welcome and signup lines that promised "personal accounts stay private" are reworded to
         "you choose which accounts to share" (true in both Couple and Advanced Couple), and the
         getting-started checklist item no longer claims everything stays private by default. */
